This directory is a VENDORED FORK of:

    @handlewithcare/prosemirror-suggest-changes
    version 0.1.8
    https://github.com/handlewithcarecollective/prosemirror-suggest-changes

It is vendored rather than depended on because the suggestion mark specs had to
be replaced wholesale (see ../../editor/suggestions/marks.ts). Under Yjs,
y-prosemirror's `gatherMarks` resolves marks BY NAME, so upstream's `insertion` /
`deletion` / `modification` names shadow y-prosemirror's own `y-attributed-*`
handling and silently corrupt authorship attribution. Our marks are named
`suggestionInsert` / `suggestionDelete` / `suggestionModify`.

Changes made to upstream 0.1.8 in this fork:

  1. Mark specs removed. Marks are looked up from the schema by the names in
     `markNames.ts`; the specs themselves are declared as Tiptap extensions in
     ../../editor/suggestions/marks.ts.
  2. `generateId.ts` (numeric/string suggestion ids) replaced by `identity.ts`.
     A suggestion is identified by the mark attrs `{ user, username, date }`,
     where `date` is bucketed to 10 minutes — the Fiduswriter convention. Two
     marks with the same identity are `Mark.eq`-equal, so a burst of edits by
     one author auto-joins into one suggestion instead of fragmenting.
  3. Every `mark.attrs["id"]` read/compare became `suggestionIdentityOf(mark)` /
     `sameSuggestion(a, b)`, and every `markType.create({ id })` became
     `markType.create({ ...identity })`.
  4. Mark lookups that used `MarkType.isInSet` (returns only the FIRST mark of a
     type) became `findSuggestionMark`, which searches the whole mark set for a
     matching identity. Without this, two authors' overlapping suggestions on
     the same text node cannot be accepted/rejected independently.
  5. Accept/reject now remove the specific `Mark` instance rather than every
     mark of that type, so one author's decision does not erase the other's.
  6. Ported from the published ESM build to TypeScript sources, importing
     ProseMirror through `@tiptap/pm/*` so there is exactly one PM instance.

Upstream license follows verbatim.

